{
  "summary": "Random weight checks for athletes are organised and are the responsibility of the IJF Education and Coaching Commission, carried out for individual events only with no random weigh-in for IJF Mixed Team events [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. For IJF World Judo Tour events the random weigh-in will open one hour before the start of the competition each day, and the time limit to arrive is 30 minutes or 6 contests before the athlete’s first contest at the latest [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. Athletes must bring their accreditation for identification, and their weight cannot be more than 5 percent higher than the official maximum weight limit of the category [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. The draw of the athletes is done by means of software on a laptop one hour before the start of the competition at the place of the IJF IT person running the competition, drawing four athletes per category except those that are plus categories [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. The list of named athletes is officially posted on the official notice board placed near the warm-up area and online in the IJF notice board Telegram group [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. Four volunteers operate the random weigh-in, with two volunteers identifying the athletes and two others proceeding with the random weigh-in in two separate private rooms, while test scales are available for the duration [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096]. Anyone not passing the random weigh-in will not be allowed to take part in the competition and will be marked as DNS or DSQ on the random weigh-in list [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096].",
  "normative_basis": "The rules for the random weigh-in are established in Sport and Organisation Rules Art. 6.3 [SOR-2026-08-P079-S096] on page 79, with additional administrative responsibility outlined in the General Weigh-in section on page 74 [SOR-2026-08-P074-S085].",
